WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:22.203
"Glumdalclitch," the king said after we moved into the palace, "you will look after Grildig, as before.

2
00:00:22.204 --> 00:00:27.052
You will have your own room in the palace and your own servants.

3
00:00:27.053 --> 00:00:33.876
I want you to continue your schooling, so you will also have a tutor."

4
00:00:33.877 --> 00:00:38.010
"Yes, Your Majesty," Glumdalclitch replied.

5
00:00:38.011 --> 00:00:41.029
"Grildig and I will learn together."

6
00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:46.754
The queen ordered the palace carpenter to make a box that I could use as a bedroom.

7
00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:52.391
"See that it is just as Grildig wants," she instructed him.

8
00:00:52.392 --> 00:00:56.328
He consulted with me about the design of my box.

9
00:00:56.329 --> 00:01:00.830
It had windows, a door, furniture, and two cupboards.

10
00:01:00.831 --> 00:01:06.230
The top lifted off so that Glumdalclitch could keep the box in good order.

11
00:01:06.231 --> 00:01:11.094
"Take a look," the carpenter said to me when the box was finished.

12
00:01:11.095 --> 00:01:14.024
"The walls and floor are padded and soft!"

13
00:01:14.025 --> 00:01:18.794
I exclaimed, admiring the thick carpets and wall coverings.

14
00:01:18.795 --> 00:01:23.356
"Thank you. That will make my box very comfortable if we travel.

15
00:01:23.357 --> 00:01:26.123
Could you also put a lock on the door, please?"

16
00:01:26.124 --> 00:01:30.162
I asked, thinking of the rats in the farmer's bedroom.

17
00:01:30.163 --> 00:01:34.543
The carpenter gave me the key after he had put the lock on the door.

18
00:01:34.544 --> 00:01:36.631
The queen enjoyed my company.

19
00:01:36.632 --> 00:01:41.363
"You will dine with me every evening," she told me.

20
00:01:41.364 --> 00:01:48.039
"You must have your own dishes and silverware, and your own table and chair."

21
00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:52.085
The things her workers made for me were just the right size.

22
00:01:52.086 --> 00:01:59.382
My table and chair were on the queen's table, and Glumdalclitch sat nearby in case I needed anything.

23
00:01:59.383 --> 00:02:06.421
"On Wednesdays I dine with the king and the whole royal family," the queen told me.

24
00:02:06.422 --> 00:02:08.883
"You must join us."

25
00:02:08.884 --> 00:02:12.785
"I would like that very much," I replied.

26
00:02:12.786 --> 00:02:16.658
The king and I met often and had lively discussions.

27
00:02:16.659 --> 00:02:24.709
When we dined together, he put my little table and chair beside the salt and pepper shakers on his table.

28
00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:29.057
One evening he said, "Tell me about England.

29
00:02:29.058 --> 00:02:34.503
How does the government of your country work, and what are its laws?"

30
00:02:34.504 --> 00:02:40.115
Another time he said, "Describe the people of England and their customs."

31
00:02:40.116 --> 00:02:45.124
I told him about the many wars England had fought on land and sea.

32
00:02:45.125 --> 00:02:49.578
I described our political parties and the conflicts between them.

33
00:02:49.579 --> 00:02:52.881
I praised our universities and great buildings.

34
00:02:52.882 --> 00:02:55.848
He always listened closely.

35
00:02:55.849 --> 00:03:00.879
One evening, I must have sounded too proud when I spoke about England.

36
00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:08.312
Laughing, the king said to his main adviser, who was sitting across the table,

37
00:03:08.313 --> 00:03:11.157
"How funny the little man is.

38
00:03:11.158 --> 00:03:15.770
Englishmen seem to think that their country is better than all others.

39
00:03:15.771 --> 00:03:19.757
Even such a tiny human has too much pride."

40
00:03:19.758 --> 00:03:21.463
My face got red.

41
00:03:21.464 --> 00:03:24.006
I did not like what the king had said.

42
00:03:24.007 --> 00:03:30.474
But, of course, I kept quiet, because mostly I did like the king.

43
00:03:30.475 --> 00:03:35.451
An unpleasant thing about Brobdingnag was the enormous insects.

44
00:03:35.452 --> 00:03:38.815
The flies were as big as English geese.

45
00:03:38.816 --> 00:03:43.169
At dinner one evening, flies bothered me constantly.

46
00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:50.319
Their humming and buzzing was unbearably loud, and they landed on my food and my body.

47
00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.899
"How disgusting!" I exclaimed.

48
00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:58.288
The king and queen laughed as I waved my sword at the flies.

49
00:03:58.289 --> 00:04:03.078
One afternoon, Glumdalclitch left me in my box on her windowsill.

50
00:04:03.079 --> 00:04:07.042
The top was open so that I could get some fresh air.

51
00:04:07.043 --> 00:04:11.366
I was eating some cake, and some bees got into my box.

52
00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:14.569
I was afraid that they would sting me to death.

53
00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:19.244
I killed four of them with my sword, but the rest got away.

54
00:04:19.245 --> 00:04:21.896
I cut the stingers from the dead bees.

55
00:04:21.897 --> 00:04:25.800
"I'll keep these stingers," I said to myself.

56
00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:34.741
"If I ever return to England, people will be amazed at their size."
